   Employees Competencies (EC) and Service Performance (SP) Among Frontline
   Employees of Hotel Industry: Are They Significantly Related?},
Journal = {ADVANCED SCIENCE LETTERS},
Year = {2018},
Volume = {24},
Number = {5},
Pages = {2990-2995},
Month = {MAY},
Note = {Annual International Conference on Social and Behavioural Sciences
   (ICSBS), Singapore, SINGAPORE, AUG 14-16, 2017},
Abstract = {The purpose of this study is to investigate the key practices of human
   resource development (HRD) employee's competencies (EC) and Service
   Performance (SP) among frontline employees of hotel industry with focus
   on East Coast Malaysia-Kelantan, Terengganu and Pahang. Previous
   literature studies suggest that service performance in organization and
   effect of employees' competencies as mediator are yet to be determined.
   Therefore, 400 respondents have been selected using stratified sampling.
   229 out of 400 questionnaires were returned from hotel industry in East
   Coast Malaysia from 3 to 5 star hotels using 5-point Likert scale. This
   study was using SPSS and Partial least Square (PLS) to analyze the data.
   The study's finding indicated that the relationship between the human
   resource development (HRD) and employees' competencies (EC) towards
   service performance (SP) of frontline employees in hotel industry was
   significant. This study hopes that the results could make a contribution
   to the hotel management, society and also enrich literature reviews in
   this area.},
