   Assoc},
Abstract = {A comparison on the existing learning platforms for blended learning was
   conducted. The platforms are categorised into two: portal based and
   virtual worlds learning platform. Portal refers to the interface where
   the information could be exchanged among the users where virtual world
   refers to platform where users could interact among them on real time
   basis, in addition to exchanging information between them. The findings
   of the comparison suggest that virtual world platform is more preferable
   for the students compared to the portal based learning platformas it is
   more engaging and it provides students with the ability to interact
   among their peers and instructors.},
