   Artificial Computation (IWINAC), Almeria, SPAIN, JUN 03-07, 2019},
Organization = {Spanish CYTED; Red Nacl Computac Nat \& Artificial, Programa Grupos
   Excelencia Fundac Seneca \& Apliquem Microones 21 s l},
Abstract = {We report the application of recurrent deep learning networks, namely
   long term short memories (LSTM) for the modeling of gait synchronization
   of legs using a basic configuration of off-the-shelf inertial
   measurement units (IMU) providing six acceleration and rotation
   parameters. The proposed system copes with noisy and missing data due to
   high sampling rate, before applying the training of LSTM. We report
   accurate testing results on one experimental subject. This model can be
   transferred to robotised prostheses and assistive robotics devices in
   order to achieve quick stabilization and robust transfer of control
   algorithms to new users.},
