   computational tools and techniques used in studies aiming to understand
   the neural substrate of the observable behavior. In this short review we
   focus on the description of available computational tools in a landscape
   of resources that is steadily growing as the scientific community
   recognizes this Computational Neuroethology as one of the frontiers of
   scientific endeavor. We comment on the biological basis and some
   examples of studies reported in the literature before providing a
   description and taxonomy of resources and tools.},
