   production of farmers in Dakrong district - a highland district of
   Central Vietnam. The study was conducted with 180 farmers, being
   selected randomly from three communes of the district. Factor analysis
   and Multinomial Logit regression indicated six main groups of factors
   impacting on four separate adaptation options (called ADP) in maize
   production in the area. In which, the increasing in household's
