   Integration of Multidisciplinarity Aspect, Medan, INDONESIA, APR 23-24,
   2018},
Abstract = {Problematic Internet Use (PIU) is considered not to have consensus
   related to theory and assessment to date. The Indonesia Problematic
   Internet Use (IPIUS) is an instrument developed based on the Davis PIU
   concept and the modification of the GPIUS2 Caplan instrument. IPUS
   consists of 63 items with 6 dimensions, namely Preference of Online
   Social Interaction (POSI), escaping, cognitive preoccupation, compulsive
   internet use, negative outcomes, and emotional reactivity. The emotional
   reactivity dimension is deemed necessary in IPIUS to consider the
   emotional problems that arise in internet use in Indonesia. The CFA test
   results indicate that IPIUS is a valid model and fit well with the data
   and it is valid to be applied for further research.},
