   International-Society-for-Ecological-Psychology, MIAMI UNIV, OXFORD,
   OHIO, MAY, 2002},
Organization = {Int Soc Ecol Psychol},
Abstract = {A theory of affordances is outlined according to which affordances are
   relations between the abilities of animals and features of the
   environment. As relations, affordances are both real and perceivable but
   are not properties of either the environment or the animal. I argue that
   this theory has advantages over extant theories of affordances and
   briefly discuss the relations among affordances and niches, perceivers,
   and events.},
