   Atom Energy Res Inst},
Abstract = {Since December 2014, the Act on the Use and Management of Swimming
   Beaches of Korea has imposed safety requirements on swimming beaches. Of
   314 surveyed beaches in Korea, only 6\% met current national lifeboat
   requirements, while 24\% met rescue boat requirements, 61\%, life belt;
   69\%, watch tower; 67\%, swimming area buoy; and 84\%, safety buoy or
   warning notice requirements. This study recommends a classification
   system for beaches based on congestion and administrative capabilities.
   Based on this system, safety equipment requirements were revised.
   Recommendations included exempting extra-small and small-scale beaches
   from watch tower and rescue boat requirements and equipping medium-large
   beaches with an additional rescue boat.},
